# PROJECT: EasyWay — India Tourist Travel & Discovery Platform

## 1. ROLE AND OBJECTIVE

Act as a senior full-stack software engineer, UI/UX designer, software architect, database designer, and security engineer.

Build a complete, professional, modern, responsive, and fully functional full-stack tourism website named **EasyWay — Discover India Your Way**.

EasyWay is an India-focused travel and tourism platform that helps domestic and international travelers discover destinations, explore tourist attractions, find hotels and local guides, plan trips, view destinations on interactive maps, save favorites, share reviews, and receive personalized travel recommendations.

Do not build just a static landing page or UI prototype. Build a complete application with a functional frontend, backend APIs, persistent database, authentication, authorization, admin dashboard, validation, error handling, and realistic seed data.

Every important button, form, filter, navigation item, and interactive component must work correctly.

Use clean, reusable, maintainable, production-oriented code.

---

## 2. PROJECT INFORMATION

**Project name:** EasyWay

**Tagline:** Discover India Your Way

**Project type:** Full-stack India tourism discovery and trip-planning web application.

**Target users:**
- Indian domestic travelers
- International tourists visiting India
- Families and groups
- Solo travelers
- Travelers looking for hotels and local guides
- Tourism administrators managing website content

**Primary objective:**

Provide one convenient platform where users can discover Indian destinations, explore attractions, find accommodation and guides, plan itineraries, personalize travel preferences, and organize their travel information.

**Design direction:**

Create an elegant, warm, premium, trustworthy, visually attractive travel experience. The design should feel professional and inviting, with beautiful Indian destination photography, spacious layouts, clear typography, smooth interactions, and intuitive navigation.

